Here's a skincare myth I used to believe: that percentages are all-important with active ingredients.

The truth isn't so simple! There's a lot of other factors that determine how much of the amount they originally put into the product actually makes it into the skin, to where it needs to be to work.

Shoutout to the excellent @eviesamuel_ for inspiring me to revisit myths I used to believe - she's a great follow for sensible and scientific skincare takes, and A+ product recommendations!

I go through more myths I used to believe in my latest YT video - let me know what beauty myths you used to believe!

